  "publication_target": null,
  "pitch": null,
  "ml_idea": "The project considered was: predict each variant's effect on a depression-disease shared-liability factor (or classify shared versus disease-specific variants) from DNA sequence embeddings and functional annotations, held out by chromosome. It fails A8 because the target is produced by genomic structural equation modelling from 24 publicly downloadable GWAS, so the obvious features reconstruct the label; and with sequence-only features the target is governed by linkage disequilibrium and each input GWAS's sample size rather than by variant biology. The only decision anyone actually wants - which depressed patient develops cardiometabolic disease - needs individual-level biobank genotypes, which are controlled access and are not in this release.",
  "effort": {"hours_to_feature_table": 25, "working_set_gb": 3.5, "needs_gpu": false, "peak_ram_gb": 4, "embedding_hours": null, "cv_run_minutes": 20, "compute_note": "Estimated, not timed: 2.4 GB of gzipped summary statistics read per chromosome, joined to annotation tracks; a gradient-boosting baseline on ~1-2k loci runs in minutes. Sequence-model embeddings would add a GPU day.", "cheapest_killing_check": "Regress each factor's per-SNP Z on a weighted sum of the constituent disease GWAS Z-scores (download links are in Supplementary Table 1). If the R-squared is near 1, the label is reconstructible from freely available features and the supervised framing is circular."},
  "verdict": "reject",
  "verdict_reason": "Fails A8 (label provenance). Every candidate target in this release - the per-SNP factor beta/Z, the Q-SNP class, the TWAS gene hits, the pathway and cell-type scores - is the output of a statistical model (genomic SEM, FUSION, MAGMA, GSA-MiXeR, gsMAP) fitted to 24 public GWAS, not a measurement. The natural feature set is those same GWAS, which reconstructs the label by linear combination, so the task is circular by construction; with sequence-only features the target is driven by linkage disequilibrium and GWAS sample size rather than biology. A1-A7 pass: the data is genuinely open (CC BY 4.0 figshare, columns documented, GRCh37 stated), but the effective sample size is ~1,019 independent loci, not 6.5 million rows, and the field (FLAMES, V2D, AlphaGenome) is already crowded with recent, honestly evaluated variant-prioritisation models."
}
